#F02 - Unauthorised Administrator Account Registration
DRAFT

## Summary

I identified a broken access-control issue in the application's registration
endpoint, 'POST /api/Users'. An unauthenticated user can supply a privileged
role value in the registration request. When the request body includes
"role": "admin", the application returns
'201 Created' and creates an account with administrator privileges.

The application appears to trust a client-controlled role field instead of
assigning the default role on the server. The issue was validated in an
authorised lab environment by signing in with the newly created account and
confirming administrator access.

**Severity:**

High  

**Affected component:**

Registration endpoint: POST /api/Users

**Classification:**

OWASP Top 10:2025 A01 - Broken Access Control
CWE-266 - Incorrect Privilege Assignment

---

## Discovery

During testing of the registration workflow, I intercepted the account-creation
request with Burp Suite. The HTTP response indicated that newly created
accounts used the "role":"customer" role. This suggested that the role was included in
the client-server registration flow.

picture

I then created a new test account and changed the JSON role property
from the standard customer value to 'admin'. The endpoint accepted the request
and returned '201 Created'. Authentication with the resulting account confirmed
that it was able to access administrator functionality.

picture
picture


