## Steps to Reproduce

1. In an authorised test environment, open the application's registration page.
2. Configure the browser to proxy traffic through Burp Suite and enable
   interception.
3. Submit a registration form using a new test identity.
4. Locate the intercepted 'POST /api/Users' request.

picture

5. In the JSON object, replace the ordinary role value with the
   following property: "role": "admin"
(it must not be placed inside 'securityQuestion' as it does not modify the account role (was an error I made)

picture

6. Forward the modified request.
7. Observe that the server responds with '201 Created'.

picture

8. Sign in using the newly created test account and verify that administrator
   functionality is available (do not forget to turn of the proxy interception)

picture



